Subject: [REVIEW 07/09] DisplayPort tunneling, FEC and DSC startup

Integrate the USB4 provider with DP startup/shutdown, AUX/segmented EDID, FEC readiness and acknowledgment, DSC selection, and interrupt/clock sequencing. Review all failure paths and native-DP behavior. Native HPD notifications are handled in a worker, so the notifier never waits for AUX, and a withdrawn HPD stops AUX transfers to the departed sink.

Dependencies: Patch 05 supplies the usb4-dp.h provider interface and patch 06 the DPU side. Patch 02 is a runtime dependency rather than a symbol reference: dp_ctrl.c sets the DP input link clock rate, which needs the writable dispcc divider from 02 through the board clock bindings in 08-09. Patches 05-07 form a coupled host/display integration, not independently validated features.

Source attribution: Local Surface integration; provenance/usb4/21-drm-msm-dp-propagate-host-phy-init-errors.patch, provenance/display/ DSC/FEC deltas and provenance/derivation.json.

This is a review grouping of preserved source, not a new authorship claim or
an independently build-validated upstream commit. Original attribution remains
in the referenced provenance files. No new Signed-off-by trailers are added.

